Description: native GNOME photograph culling and selection suite
 Photo Selector Linux is a native GNOME photograph culling and comparison
 application for Debian 13 (Trixie) and other current Linux desktops.
 .
 Key features:
  * 1-Up, 2-Up, and 3-Up Focus Mode with tactile Sliding Triplet navigation
  * Noise-corrected 2D Laplacian focus sharpness scoring
  * Move, Copy and Trash operations with undo; originals stay in place on Copy
  * Native Libadwaita dark theme and keyboard-driven culling
  * Support for camera RAW formats, JPEG companions, and XMP sidecars
